+135. Reference Flow
+
+USER → INTENT → GOAL → PLAN → DECISION
+  ↓
+AUTHORIZATION / CAPABILITY LEASE DECISION
+  ↓
+DURABLE PRE-EXECUTION PERMISSION DECISION + IMMUTABLE AUDIT REFERENCE
+  ├─ DENIED → DURABLE DENIAL FACT → AUDIT / CHRONICLE
+  │           (NO TOOL EXECUTION; NO WORLD COMMIT)
+  └─ GRANTED → ACTION → TOOL / MCP → EXTERNAL WORLD
+                ↓
+              DURABLE EXECUTION / OBSERVATION / EVIDENCE FACTS
+                ↓
+              EXTERNAL-EFFECT RECONCILIATION WHEN NEEDED
+                ├─ UNKNOWN, UNRESOLVED → DURABLE UNKNOWN FACT
+                │                         → RECOVERY_REQUIRED / ESCALATION
+                │                         (NO BLIND RETRY; NO WORLD SUCCESS)
+                └─ RESOLVED → VERIFICATION
+                               ↓
+                             DURABLE VerificationReceipt
+                               ├─ FAILED / STALE / CONFLICT
+                               │  → DURABLE FAILURE FACT / AUDIT / CHRONICLE
+                               │    (NO SUCCESSFUL WORLD OUTCOME)
+                               └─ PASS → EXACT-PARENT APPLICABILITY CHECK
+                                          ↓
+                                 WORLD KERNEL CAS ATOMIC COMMIT
+                                ┌────────────────────────────────┐
+                                │ Resulting canonical World     │
+                                │ version                        │
+                                │ Immutable WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT │
+                                │ Durable committed-outcome      │
+                                │ delivery intent (created here) │
+                                └────────────────────────────────┘
+                                          ↓
+                              POST-COMMIT EVENT FABRIC DELIVERY
+                                          ↓
+                              DELIVERY ATTEMPT / ACK / REDELIVERY
+                                          ↓
+                              DURABLE OUTCOME FACT / CHRONICLE
+                              (BOUND TO WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT)
+
+The pre-execution audit, precommit execution/observation/verification facts,
+failure and UNKNOWN facts, World Kernel commit, and post-commit successful
+outcome are DISTINCT lifecycle records. Truthful precommit facts MAY reach
+Chronicle before World commit but NEVER assert completed modeled-World success.
+The Event / Trace Fabric and Chronicle hold historical evidence and traces;
+neither may commit a World version or infer an external effect from delivery.
+
+The CAS triple is an all-or-none World authority boundary. The committed-event
+delivery intent is durable inside that boundary; actual delivery and
+acknowledgement occur after it and are not guaranteed exactly once.
+Denied, failed, stale and unresolved external-effect paths remain durable
+without requiring a fabricated WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT.
 
